      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the polar curve $r=12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ?$",
      "worked_solution": "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(0,a).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{12}{2}=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|6|=6$ centered at the point $(0,6),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14225098/assets/adf3c76c7b9bcb1d1c8a917716bf6df70cf456d03db4ef8759b049686975bae3.png)",
